# IOI desk
#
# Shows:   the market side sending IOIs and adverts from `run` blocks — `ioi`,
#          `replace ioi`, `cancel ioi`, `advert`, `replace advert`,
#          `cancel advert` — and minding IOIs sent by hand with `on sent ioi`
# Needs:   any active session; run it on LOOP-MKT with ioi-taker running on
#          LOOP-CLI to see the orders come back
# Watch:   Sent IOIs and Sent Adverts (Market menu): the IOIRefID moving as
#          each replace and cancel lands; Received IOIs on the client side
# Outcome: three IOIs go out a second apart, each replaced up after two
#          seconds and cancelled two seconds later; one advert is sent,
#          replaced and cancelled; an IOI sent by hand is cancelled after
#          ten seconds

seed 3

# A `run` block that sends IOIs is a market block: what it sends is what it
# is about, and `ioi.…` is its row. Each pass of the `repeat` is one IOI's
# macro.
run
    repeat 3 every 1s with sym = ['IBM', 'MSFT', 'AAPL']
        ioi symbol: sym, side: buy, qty: 'L', price: TICK(20 + n, 0.01), quality: high, natural: yes,
        after 2s
        # Terms left out keep the IOI's values: only the size and price change.
        replace ioi qty: 'M', price: TICK(ioi.price + 0.05, 0.01)
        after 2s
        cancel ioi text: 'done ${ioi.ioi_id}'
        pass 'IOI chain ended at ${ioi.ioi_id}'

run
    advert symbol: 'IBM', side: trade, qty: 5000, price: 20.5, last_mkt: 'XNAS'
    after 1s
    replace advert qty: 6000
    after 1s
    cancel advert
    pass 'advertised ${advert.quantity} ${advert.symbol}'

# An IOI sent from the Sent IOIs blotter by hand, on the session this run
# was started on.
on sent ioi
    after 10s
    if ioi.status == 'Active'
        cancel ioi text: 'stale'
